# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DB FinCo — environment variables
#
# Copy to .env.local for development, or set these in the Vercel project
# settings for a deployment. Every variable here is optional: the site builds
# and runs correctly with none of them set.
#
# NEVER commit real values. .env* files are git-ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Public origin of the deployed site.
# Used for canonical URLs, Open Graph URLs, the sitemap and structured data.
#
# OPTIONAL. All of the following are treated identically as "not configured",
# and fall back to https://dbfinco.com:
#   - the variable is absent
#   - the variable is set to an empty string   (what Vercel stores for a blank value)
#   - the variable contains only whitespace
#
# A non-empty but malformed value (no scheme, or a scheme other than http/https)
# also falls back to the default and prints a build-time warning, rather than
# failing the build.
#
# The value is normalised: whitespace trimmed, trailing slash, query string and
# fragment removed. Both of these therefore resolve to https://dbfinco.com:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://dbfinco.com/
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=  https://dbfinco.com/?utm=x
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://dbfinco.com

# Optional external scheduling link (e.g. a booking tool).
# When set, every "Schedule a Free Consultation" button points here.
# When unset, those buttons link to /contact — never a dead link.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form delivery (Resend)
#
# The form works without these: submissions are validated server-side and the
# visitor is told honestly that the message was not delivered, with the phone
# number and email addresses offered instead. It never shows a false success.
#
# Set BOTH RESEND_API_KEY and CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL to enable real delivery.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# API key from https://resend.com — server-side only, never exposed to the browser.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Verified sender address on your Resend domain, e.g. website@dbfinco.com
CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=

# Where enquiries are delivered. Defaults to enquiry@dbfinco.com when unset.
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=enquiry@dbfinco.com
